# Default-deny. The build context is the lock file and the source, nothing else.
# An allowlist cannot silently start shipping something the way a deny-list can
# the moment a new directory appears — and the things that must never enter the
# image are exactly the ones that grow: models/ (265MB, the image downloads its
# own copy at the pinned revision), training/ and data/ (dead weight and extra
# attack surface in a runtime image), .git/, and the local .venv/.
*
!requirements.lock
!src/

# ...except caches, which src/ would otherwise drag in.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
